cff-version: 1.3.0
message: "If you use Secure LSL in your research, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Secure LSL"
abstract: >-
  Secure LSL is a drop-in replacement for liblsl that adds a transparent,
  unified encryption layer to the Lab Streaming Layer.
  It provides Ed25519 device authorization, per-session X25519 key exchange with
  a BLAKE2b key-derivation function, and ChaCha20-Poly1305 authenticated
  encryption, so existing LSL applications gain end-to-end security without code
  changes.
  A clean-room liblsl-ESP32 reimplementation extends the same encryption to
  microcontroller-class biosensors.
